body:
Just below this call, each head's PV row is copied into a stack `tensor` before `fma`: 16 x 512 B = 8 KB of memcpy per dense page visit at 16 heads. `fma` and `set` take any `expression`, and a `const_view` over the row satisfies it, so the copy could go:

    tron::const_view<float, true, false, tron::seq<operation_head_size>> row{
        amx_o + offset * operation_head_size};

and `row` goes where `scratch` went. `amx_o` is 64-byte aligned and the row offset is a multiple of 512 B, so the aligned view is sound.

Checked by: `sed -n 1795,1797p h/tron/models/self_attention.hpp` -> `tensor<operation_head_size> scratch; std::memcpy(...)` inside the `offset < operation_kv_mul` loop; `fma` takes any `expression` at `expr.hpp:537-542` and `const_view` derives from `expr` at `view.hpp:361-362`.

