"keeps unused rows zero" reads as a design reason, but nothing consumes rows `>= group_heads` of `o`: the call site loops `offset < operation_kv_mul`, the numerics test loops `qi < group_heads`, and output row i depends on P row i only. The property that does matter is per-instantiation storage, so a 4-head call never sees a 16-head call's rows, and the Note relies on that.

```suggestion
  // A function template's thread_local exists once per instantiation, so a
  // 4-head call never sees a 16-head call's rows; Note [Tile stores write 16
  // rows] relies on that for its zero-row claim.
```

